## About the standard

SSF 130 provides rules for the design, installation, testing, and documentation of intruder and hold-up alarms. It distinguishes alarm classes 1–4 according to the system requirements.

Alarm classes apply to the alarm system, not the building's physical protection, which is addressed by SSF 200. Customers and insurance terms often determine the required classes for a particular site.

Official source: [SSF 130 utgåva 10](https://www.stoldskyddsforeningen.se/butik/foretag/ssf-normer/inbrottslarm/ssf-130-utg-10-projektering-och-installation-av-inbrotts-och-overfallslarmanlaggning/).
